{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain","id":1486252,"title":"[Project] Make an Anarch domain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-11T22:06:51-07:00","id":1486252,"title":"[Project] Make an Anarch domain","content":"One of the biggest problems with the Anarchs is not so much that they're uninteresting but they stand against rather than for. We know what a Camarilla domain looks like because Chicago by Night provided the Prince/Primogen/Harpies template. However, LA by Night failed to really convey what an Anarch domain should be like with the Barons just being, &quot;Prince in miniature.&quot; So this is a thread where we share ideas of how exactly an Anarch domain might be governed and maybe even some ideas about how they should function.<br /> <br /> Go into as much detail or as little detail as you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:24:07-07:00","id":1486254,"title":"","content":"It's a smaller city<br /> There's a prince<br /> But he doesn't like the Camarilla because he likes Roads","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:25:40-07:00","id":1486255,"title":"","content":"Although the game doubled down on the idea of the Movement as a sect of its own, I think an &quot;Anarch Domain&quot; would be less of a Domain under sect control and more a Domain where the Camarilla lost to the local rebels and... those rebels built whatever made sense for them in the specific case. Those may be a huge variety of things, including actually Domains that are still Camarilla, but under big concessions or a locally appointed and popular Prince. At most such Domains could offer some limited support for Anarchs elsewhere and be standing examples that the Revolution is possible, but their actual individual workings would hardly be inspiring to many outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:28:50-07:00","id":1486256,"title":"","content":"In my rendition of San Jose the Anarchs moved in and set up a Council. Coteries with enough size or influence get a seat on the council while those who are not part of a coterie choose a representative to speak on their behalf and cast a vote for them.<br /> <br /> When the Anarchs arrived en masse and set up they issued an invitation to the Camarilla that was already there to have a seat and a vote as part of the &quot;Camarilla Coterie.&quot; The Ivory Tower has yet to accept their seat. The Wan Kuei also have a seat.<br /> <br /> Also, while a kindred may own a building, buildings, or haven, none claim ownership of a domain. This irks the Camarilla something fierce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 07-12-2022, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:35:37-07:00","id":1486257,"title":"","content":"Here's some things I created for my own Anarch games.<br /> <br /> <b>Pact Lands</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No one can hurt my brother other than me.&quot;</i><br /> -Yani, Ravnos, 10th generation<br /> <br /> A Pact domain is something of a variant on &quot;rulership by coterie.&quot; Basically, a Pact is an Anarch domain in the most literal sense in there is almost no law whatsoever beyond the Masquerade. However, the Pact gives free right of feeding and Creation as long as one observes the conditions of a mutual agreement between all the other Kindred. In general, a pact that agrees the various Kindred of the domain will lend their power to driving out all Camarilla, Sabbat, Blood Cults, or other rivals as well as give shelter to the other members. Some even have complicated Magna Cartas or Constitutions.<br /> <br /> In general, Pact Lands are inherently unstable but not for the usual reasons. Inevitably, one vampire becomes &quot;first among equals&quot; or more powerful than all of the others and becomes Prince or Baron. Either that or the others install a puppet while ruling as a coterie over the lessers of their rank.<br /> <br /> <b>Gladhand Domains</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I promise that every Kindred gets at least one free killing per year. My opponent is insane about how accidents should never happen. Do you want her in?&quot;</i><br /> -Glorious Gary, 10th generation Ventrue<br /> <br /> Gladhand Domains are the Kindred's most derided but still-practiced wildly groups due to the fact they practice the most ridiculous form of government for the Damned: democracy. Gladhand Domains generally elect their Mayors, Presidents, CEOs, or Barons once per year or decade depending on the age of the average Kindred involved.<br /> <br /> Gladhand Domains are derisively called this due to the simple fact that democracy among vampires is inherently ridiculous. The vast majority of Gladhand Domains are inevitably ruled by Toreador, Ventrue, or Brujah with the general assumption that whoever has the most powerful Presence will rule. Bribes are also very common as are threats with the general result being a rubber stamp on whatever the strongest Kindred rules. Blood Bonds are also not uncommon with them frequently forced on &quot;outliers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ironically, Gladhand Domains are still reasonably popular. After all, if the populace is happy, does it matter how its achieved?<br /> <br /> <b>Renunciation Domains</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We are all equal brothers and sisters before the blood. Yes, I used to work for the Ministry. Wait, don't go!&quot;</i><br /> -Carissa, self-proclaimed Caitiff<br /> <br /> Called &quot;Caitiff Kingdoms&quot; or more derisively &quot;Godless Lands&quot;, Renunciation Domains are domains where the locals have forbidden the Traditions, Clans, Generation, and any mythology of their kind. All are officially Caitiff and they are equals before the domain. Renunciation Domains generally are fairly good at avoiding Barons, Princes, and Primogen. They are, instead, nightmares of personal intrigue and behind the scenes favor trading that leaves it opaque as to who is actually in charge if anyone. Renunciation domains very often hold &quot;Rants&quot; to judge Kindred among their number via mass-decision.<br /> <br /> The mob controls these lands and whoever controls the mob. As a general rule, Renunciation Domains tend to be founded by Caitiff or outcasts of other Kindred who proceed to find themselves overwhelmed with Thin Bloods or other Clanless as Embraces pile up. They either eventually become isolationist or proceed to appoint their own Scourges and population control that often make them even more hostile to newcomers than other more traditionally-ruled lands.<br /> <br /> <b>Coplands</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am the law.&quot;</i><br /> -Bill Plickens, 9th generation Gangrel<br /> <br /> Bizarrely, a large number of Embraced cops drift toward the Anarchs. This is not something that is lost on many Brujah who have as much a tradition of turning law enforcement as they do radical revolutionaries. Cops are frequently angry, violent, and full of their own ideologies that attract the Learned Clan. The Camarilla appeals to some but others find the Anarchs just need their special touch--especially if their members are more pragmatic revolutionaries than nihilistic rabble. Other times, preexisting Anarch territories note that they absolutely despise leaders but that the chaos of their existences demands SOMEONE handle the ass-beating necessary to keep order.<br /> <br /> Coplands, simply put, don't have Princes but <i>do</i> have Sheriffs who effectively serve as the whole of the law. They and their deputies wield the power normally afforded to the Prince and Primogen with the power to interpret the law as they see fit. Many Anarchs derisively compare them to the small hick small town Sheriff domains that used to rid the South or even compare them to Chicago's Balthazar.<br /> <br /> Bizarrely, Coplands are fairly stable Anarch domains despite how much they're against the typical Anarch screed. More &quot;moderate&quot; Anarchs appreciate the relative straightforwardness of their society than in the constant backstabbing of Camarilla courts. They're tyrannies but you know where you stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-12-2022, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T04:11:46-07:00","id":1486269,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I have a thought for a domain patterned after traditional monastic rules, but I'll have to do some reading first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T04:25:06-07:00","id":1486271,"title":"","content":"'while a kindred may own a building, building, or haven, none claim ownership of a domain'<br /> <br /> but how is it not a domain if the building or haven is owed by a vampire? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T04:51:46-07:00","id":1486273,"title":"","content":"in anarchs unbound there a short story about a sire and her childe who are anarchs they managed to overthrow the camarilla in their and the sire explains how they are going to rule the city and the childe puts out that her sire just recreated the same system they had just gotten rid of, I kinda like the idea that for all of their idealism anarchs either allow their domains to fall into anarchy or they become like the camarilla without being in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T09:28:53-07:00","id":1486285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain?p=1486255#post1486255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the game doubled down on the idea of the Movement as a sect of its own, I think an &quot;Anarch Domain&quot; would be less of a Domain under sect control and more a Domain where the Camarilla lost to the local rebels and... those rebels built whatever made sense for them in the specific case.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost the book definition of an Anarch domain.<br /> <br /> The overall city should be in short diving distance to a city that is under the Camarillo thumb. Think of something like the Minneapolis and St. Paul, or Dallas and Ft. Worth, or San Francisco and San Jose. This is to set up a situation where the vampires of each city can keep fucking with each other, to the point they are all more paranoid than even vampires are normally. <br /> <br /> The anarch city is divided up into fiefdom, with vampire affairs in each being run differently. Some are highly libertarian, some are arcane, some are socialist, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T10:01:05-07:00","id":1486288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain?p=1486271#post1486271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'while a kindred may own a building, building, or haven, none claim ownership of a domain'<br /> <br /> but how is it not a domain if the building or haven is owed by a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it Domain has always been a matter of turf or territory. There is a difference between owning a building and controlling a block or district.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T10:39:16-07:00","id":1486289,"title":"","content":"<b>Old Skool Domainz</b><br /> <br /> Those Domains have a common set of laws, but instead of focusing on Masquerade and such, the focus are the rules for the claim of territory. Every Kindred or Coterie (depending on local relationships and practical consideration) is afforded the rights to claim a territory they have a right to govern and obligation to protect.<br /> <br /> Such codes can be simple or byzantine, but they usually give a limit to size for such territories, rigidly set or not, like &quot;a plot of land you can watch from your haven&quot;, and an overall idea of what kind of protection is expected from the territory holders. Signs of some sort are used to mark territories, and some such Domains have a central record with territories, their Lords and their &quot;heraldry and sigils&quot;.<br /> <br /> As long as you don't cause trouble for other territories, you're the lord of your own. You can deal with invaders however you see fit, you extend hospitality to whomever and whenever you want, and set whatever laws you wanna try. If someone tries to fuck the system, their territory is forfeited until they're dealt with by mob justice from all the territories..<br /> <br /> Most such Domains are quiet from the vampire perspective at a first glance. The system is meant to make Kindred spend as much time as possible in their own territories, minding their own businesses. They may have an Elysium-like space to meet in neutral ground, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Under the surface, though, a problem is obvious: most territories won't have all the resources they need. Prized mortals and institutions wander about, crossing territories and leaving your &quot;protection&quot;. Food and shelter may be plenty or scarce, territories of equal size are not of equal value. The rules of Prestation are the laws of survival, as negotiating with your neighbors is a necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:03:35-07:00","id":1486294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain?p=1486289#post1486289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Old Skool Domainz</b><br /> <br /> Those Domains have a common set of laws, but instead of focusing on Masquerade and such, the focus are the rules for the claim of territory. Every Kindred or Coterie (depending on local relationships and practical consideration) is afforded the rights to claim a territory they have a right to govern and obligation to protect.<br /> <br /> Such codes can be simple or byzantine, but they usually give a limit to size for such territories, rigidly set or not, like &quot;a plot of land you can watch from your haven&quot;, and an overall idea of what kind of protection is expected from the territory holders. Signs of some sort are used to mark territories, and some such Domains have a central record with territories, their Lords and their &quot;heraldry and sigils&quot;.<br /> <br /> As long as you don't cause trouble for other territories, you're the lord of your own. You can deal with invaders however you see fit, you extend hospitality to whomever and whenever you want, and set whatever laws you wanna try. If someone tries to fuck the system, their territory is forfeited until they're dealt with by mob justice from all the territories..<br /> <br /> Most such Domains are quiet from the vampire perspective at a first glance. The system is meant to make Kindred spend as much time as possible in their own territories, minding their own businesses. They may have an Elysium-like space to meet in neutral ground, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Under the surface, though, a problem is obvious: most territories won't have all the resources they need. Prized mortals and institutions wander about, crossing territories and leaving your &quot;protection&quot;. Food and shelter may be plenty or scarce, territories of equal size are not of equal value. The rules of Prestation are the laws of survival, as negotiating with your neighbors is a necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice write-up! Presumably there's a method for determining how to protect the city as a whole from the Sabbat or other possible invaders but for the most part, I assume that individual Cainites are up to themselves to protecting their turf.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the need for expansion will be a temptation for individual Kindred who are stuck with territory that isn't as nice as their neighbors.<br /> <br /> Because, well, Kindred are greedy bastards by nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:32:35-07:00","id":1486299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain?p=1486294#post1486294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice write-up! Presumably there's a method for determining how to protect the city as a whole from the Sabbat or other possible invaders but for the most part, I assume that individual Cainites are up to themselves to protecting their turf.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the need for expansion will be a temptation for individual Kindred who are stuck with territory that isn't as nice as their neighbors.<br /> <br /> Because, well, Kindred are greedy bastards by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had those things in mind while writing, but going into too much detail seemed unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Those &quot;expected protections&quot;? If the Sabbat is a looming threat, keeping an eye open and capturing spies may be one such expectation and a quick way for those who can't watch their turf to lose it. If some turfs are more prone to attack than others, there may even be a local combination for a Blood Tithe for the holders of such turfs, or some other compensation for their work.<br /> <br /> On the other side, some Domains work for the story because they're badly managed, and those are no exception. Some may have a lot of care in making providence against larger threats, but others may not notice they're running on the good will of their neighbors, Anarch or Camarilla, and are basically a catastrophic failure waiting to happen because of their excessive insularity. Something will go wrong, and they won't have the will to work together to deal with it.<br /> <br /> And yes, of course those are all prone to abuse, specially when Prestation goes from a &quot;currency&quot; to the main system to have the basic things working. Ambitious Kindred will always find a way to gobble better turf or crush neighbors with debt, and as long as that doesn't fuck the whole system, there's no recourse to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:45:33-07:00","id":1486302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486252-project-make-an-anarch-domain?p=1486271#post1486271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but how is it not a domain if the building or haven is owed by a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot comment on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar490_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"490\" data-vbnamecard=\"490\">omenseer</a> game, I want to make a general point as this issue is something that often gets raised. It certainly does by players in my gaming group. So I want to make a general comment on how I handle this in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> There is a distinction between private property and the use or jurisdiction of any kind of political power or privilege over it. &quot;Domain&quot; in Vampire does not mean one's private property. It means the exercise of political power under the Traditions. It's the difference between someone in the 21st century owning an old aristocratic manor as his personal home, and the actual feudal lord who lived there with actual political power over the people - both serf and free - in his domain during the 12th century.<br /> <br /> &quot;Domain&quot; is often used quite liberally by players to mean anything they control or influence. In the chronicles I run, I try to distinguish the domain of the Prince versus anything a vampire may exclusively control. I call &quot;recognized&quot; claims, meaning a &quot;sub-domain&quot; that has acknowledgement of the Prince, &quot;Estates&quot;. If you have an exclusive feeding territory that others cannot enter, and the Prince openly acknowledges you or your coterie have exclusive feeding rights there, it is an &quot;estate&quot;. If the Prince doesn't recognize it, well you don't have any support from the Prince if someone violates your claim - it's a normal vampire turf war. Most players would call that &quot;their domain&quot;, but I don't because it is still the Prince that has that domain. He is putting his own support behind it in some fashion, meaning he could punish someone who attempts to violate it. <br /> <br /> &quot;Estates&quot; are most often feeding territory, but can sometimes include other things like influence in certain institutions. This is most often done in a negative way - the Prince informs everyone that nobody can have influence over the police for example - rather than the Prince positively acknowledging another person's exclusive right to have influence somewhere. But this does happen. in CbN we're told that Doyle &quot;controls&quot; the stockyards, that Tyler &quot;controls&quot; the airports, that Drummond &quot;controls&quot; the railroads and so on. These seem to be things that other vampires acknowledge.<br /> <br /> Now a certain amount of possessions are customarily acknowledged, but it's more in terms of &quot;every man is king of his own castle&quot;. One's haven, one's ghouls, most personal possessions - not necessarily one's private property - and so on are supposed to be respected by other Kindred. Vampires aren't serfs in the Camarilla. (Again, individual vampires may think this is part of their &quot;domain&quot;, but it isn't.) But these amount of protections are much less as a vampire in vampire society, than mortals in mortal society.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another distinction that should be made is between property rights recognized by mortals, and what vampires recognize. Simply put, vampires don't recognize mortal law as applying to them at all. It's like a farmer putting what his livestock thinks or wants before his own needs. It doesn't matter to the farmer if the sheep does not want to be sheared. It gets sheared.<br /> <br /> Now there is probably some customary measures over what a vampire owned as a mortal still belonging to him, but only if there wasn't some previous vampire claim over it. I've had more than one PC suddenly realize that his company was already part of some other vampire's influence with that vampire already having agents - bonded, dominated, or some other means - inside it. So which vampire &quot;owns&quot; it? The elder vampire who already &quot;owned&quot; that, or the new neonate whose mortal identity owns it by mortal law? Now in these cases, the Prince is usually happy to step in and arbitrate a solution. The neonate will preserve something, as long as the interests of the elder are protected.<br /> <br /> We see something similar in CbN with Drummond and his &quot;control&quot; over the railroads. Now, what does that mean? Anyone can buy a ticket, right? So most vampire PCs don't see any reason why they need to pay something else (like boons, or some other arrangement) to Drummond to use it. That worked fine in minor circumstances. Drummond knew it was foolish to try to stop anyone who just wanted to travel within the city or to nearby suburbs and back. But the PCs learned on a longer trip outside Chicago going to another city that the train had a &quot;malfunction&quot; that stopped it, threatening they'd not make their destination before sunrise, and that - oops - their luggage was lost. Of course, one of the heavily conditioned railroad employees told them that his master could fix everything if only they could come to agreement with him. Since the game was taking place in the 1920s before air travel or the interstate highway system was established, they didn't have too many other options but to come to some sort of agreement.<br /> <br /> Humans got to use the railroad by paying the ticket price because that's the equivalent of letting one's cows out to pasture. Vampires need to come to some sort of terms because they're &quot;people&quot; (unlike humans) wanting to use his property (the rail network).<br /> <br /> The same thing would happen if people wanted to use the airports, it's just that they would need to make arrangements with Tyler instead.<br /> <br /> Players hate this of course. It seems unfair to them. They want the old rules that applied (when they were livestock who could get eaten at any time) instead of the new rules (which protects them under the Traditions). And they'll do everything they can to avoid making such deals and finding alternate means. That's fine too. It's expected. Drive a car instead of using the railroad. (This is why Drummond's power collapsed after the 1950s - the railroads weren't essential anymore to vampires wanting to travel.) <br /> <br /> And smart vampires who &quot;control&quot; such things make sure that the cost (boons) to use them is within reason (like trivial boons for single use, or a minor boon to cover most personal travel over the long term, only getting to major if there really is some kind major effort to accommodate some special need or service) and that they must provide excellent service in exchange. So most vampires get pacified especially once they learn that this is typical, and that the vampire in question actually CAN deny them the use of these services (by various means). Paying one minor boon for access, or one or more trivial boons isn't THAT much of a cost. Of course, over time a lot of trivial and minor boons can be collected and called in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't like it? Well, this is one reason why some vampires go Anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T12:22:53-07:00","id":1486304,"title":"","content":"Any bloodline or clan may be found in an anarch domaine. You might find a Giovanni spy who is pretending to have run away from the clan, a Salubri avoiding the Tremere, a Bali pretending to be most any other clan at all and so on. Standard members of the Gangrel, the Ministry, and the Bruhjah are among the Anarch, as are the outliers of the normal clans. <br /> <br /> Anything goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T14:46:17-07:00","id":1486310,"title":"","content":"I think two things should be remembered when doing an Anarch Domain:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>They should be distinct enough not to be the Camarilla 2.0</b>: The fact that Anarch domains can rapidly become &quot;Camarilla lite&quot; was brought above and this is true but it should still have enough differences that it's not a complete joke. If nothing else, &quot;We have the power and they don't&quot; is actually a fair argument for a vampire.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>They should be seriously flawed</b>: The Camarilla is a source of many fun adventures because it is a flawed and terrible system. Which means the Anarchs should also be flawed and terrible. There's no such thing as a vampire paradise after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T21:01:46-07:00","id":1486321,"title":"","content":"<b>Rust Kingdoms</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Gary, Indiana may not look like much but it's ours.&quot;</i><br /> -Arthur Caldwell, 9th generation Malkavian<br /> <br /> Rust Kingdoms are the most among common Anarch domains as there was a simple realization among the Anarchs of America, Australia, and other locations that there was a massive feud among Kindred for the greatest of domains: London, Paris, Chicago, New York, LA, and so on. However, there is actually a lot of SHITTY domains. The Gary, Indianas and other Rust Belt Cities actually had advantages that other more populace domains did.<br /> <br /> These lands largely tend to surround larger cities so Anarchs have access to them but they are mostly ignored by the Princes as &quot;flyover country.&quot; Rust Kingdoms are conspicuously dangerous as a large vampire population will be noticed FAR quicker by independent Hunters as well as having much larger percentages of werewolves. They also tend to be much easier to dominate and are less monitored by the Second Inquisition. They do not tend to be large numbers of Kindred but a gang of 7-12 Kindred is not uncommon.<br /> <br /> Rust Kingdoms tend to pop up in places that already have preexisting economic anxiety and tensions that allow death to go unnoticed. They are also places that Anarchs are the most obviously the same thing all vampires are: a plague on the locals.<br /> <br /> <b>Cornfields</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Norman Bates disposed of plenty of cars in that swamp. That's all I'm saying.&quot;</i><br /> -Dave Johnson, 13th generation Lasombra<br /> <br /> Cornfields are not really Anarch domains but Anarch outposts. Highway gas stations, Big Box stores, and large rural farms are places that usually serve only a single small coterie of vampires or perhaps even one. Cornfield Anarchs are still Anarchs, though, and provide locations where Anarchs can take refugee after being driven out of a city. Basically, when the heat gets too high or they're wanted for a Blood Hunt, Anarchs are sent to Cornfields where they stay until they figure out what new city to go to or arrangements are made. Hospitality is not extensive and boons are still traded but usually these places have a history of disposing of bodies. After all, frequent traffic and missing strangers works well for these.<br /> <br /> Cornfields also have a tendency to be run by vampires who, in the absence of true rivals, get a little &quot;strange&quot; in their beliefs. Heavily religious &quot;families&quot; worshiping Caine, Lilith, or Mithras are not uncommon.<br /> <br /> <b>No Man's Land</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don't cross 13th street, Dave, if you're flying Cammie colors.&quot;</i><br /> -Tinderbox, 10th generation Nosferatu<br /> <br /> The Camarilla ejecting the Anarchs from their rank resulted in something that had existed before but hadn't really been formalized and is now just a nightly reality of Kindred in all but the most fortified of Ivory Tower cities. Simply put: the majority of Princes do not have complete control over their own cities.<br /> <br /> A No Man's Land is what happens when the Anarchs of a city gather together in a specific domain and then eject or kill any Camarilla official that tries to subject them to their laws. More than one Prince has sent all of their Sheriffs and deputies to eliminate the Anarch presence in their domains, lost them all, and then found themselves helpless before their enemies.<br /> <br /> Generally, No Man's Lands are far less extreme with the Prince and Baron (and it's almost always a Baron) basically recognizing a detente. The cities basically become two different domains with the Anarchs and Camarilla generally sticking to their sides or avoiding any overt violence. Quite a few Princes and Barons choose to ignore their larger sect politics and carry on as they have for often centuries or carry out &quot;sham&quot; war that only target's the others enemies.<br /> <br /> This is notably the status of New York with the late Boss Callihan, who was lovers with and a puppet of Prince Panhard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-13-2022, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T07:15:40-07:00","id":1486340,"title":"","content":"<b>Network Domains</b><br /> <br /> For some Anarchs the Revolution isn't about taking over the city, anymore. Physical frontiers are outdated. What is society, power and authority, other than connections you have, the information you control and the recognition of your peers?<br /> <br /> Network Domains form around an idea and a few Kindred working to put it together. One puts together a networking application and the connections between apps to be added. One offers the servers for the data, another puts together logistical arrangements for shopping and delivery services that can move things across the world. VPN, databases, search engine, blockchain for smart contracts and trade, in cryptos and Prestation. No single piece need to be physically near each other, some don't need to even exist in physical form.<br /> <br /> Once the system gets momentum the site is a Domain of its own, ready to create havoc on the usual power structures of the Damned. Members bring information from wherever they are, helping the community to piece together the situation across the world. Those with the skills and the tools to cross information brought by members and found in the web (or their own databases) can piece together the secrets and going ons, follow the trails of Prestation, the gossips of Elysiums and pierce layers of secrecy over the true goals of Princes all over the place, while those who deem themselves authority on the physical world are none the wiser.<br /> <br /> The Network Domain can do more than offer a place and information to its members. It ships resources and place people, it pools ideas and expertise, it makes the political chess of the entire world easy to visualize and understand, it filters Disciplines and generation out of the social totem pole, it coordinates agents and servitors. And if the Prince itself finds out what's going on? What will they do, join the community as a <i>noob</i>?<br /> <br /> Distinctly from most Anarch Domains, Network Domains have a lot of Titles. Administrators, moderators, record keepers, fact-checkers, Anime Gif Creators, everything goes and can be coded directly in the system, so there's never doubt about who's the title holder. There are public and private spaces, each with their own encryption, and systems of layered and/or parallel hierarchies behind the initial facade of equality, ripe for exploration for those who learn to master the social system. Some are clearly structured and at the hands of the app's owners, others are wild spaces maintained by invisible watchers, and others still are bold enough to have Open Code, playing straight with the digital system, but in the hands of Kindred that specialized in gaming on-line social dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:22:32-07:00","id":1486450,"title":"","content":"A shared haven / mutual support domain (San Fernando Valley):<br /> This is a domain where a few &quot;nomadic&quot; anarch gangs take haven. They spend most on the time on the road, and only come home for healing and resting, so the area can support more vampires that it normally would. They may share some resources (haven, allies, contacts and influence) or even have a schedule for the different gangs to come home. <br /> A few vampires may have permanent residence. They help the nomad gangs keep their resources safe and in turn the gangs defend them. Mess with the domain and you will have a few gangs giving you more trouble than the small domain is worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T13:34:28-07:00","id":1486460,"title":"","content":"Based of my own setting <br /> <br /> The Republic<br /> <br /> Based on a mixture of classical athenian thought and enlightenment ideas the Republic is structured as a direct democracy. Comparatively low numbers of kindred allow for this to be quite workable on a nightly basis. The baron being more of an adjudicator and sheriff than direct ruler, were most decisions are decided by secret vote at the assembly.<br /> <br /> The domains tend to be quite resilient to Sabbat or carmarilla incursions due to the legal obligation to defend the Republic and a comparatively unified front, the Republic also tends to establish legislation to protect against eldar monopolies on power, such as limitations of domain, power and established legal rights for all kindred. However such cities often have erratic political climate where informal leaders are quickly overturned and factional infighting results in paralysed leadership.<br /> <br /> Popular in academic Liberal areas the Republic tends to surface in well entrenched brujah territories. Although a variety is beginning to emerge in Scandinavian gangrel with a 'thanes assembly&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-15-2022, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T21:14:38-07:00","id":1486490,"title":"","content":"<b>Kleptocracies</b><br /> <br /> Another type of Anarch domain that is very common is the Underworld-dominated one. Vampires have long had ties with organized crime because they are useful means of moving around cash, goods, people, and services without breaking the Masquerade. Indeed, much of the violence inherent to the Kindred condition is passed off as criminal activity. However, an interesting form of Anarch domain has emerged somewhat organically and that's where a vampire-run criminal conspiracy ends up taking over a region.<br /> <br /> The irony of kleptocracies are they don't tend to actually have been attempts to take over an area but more often end up ruling over an Anarch domain by default. Basically, a Camarilla or Sabbat presence collapses due to internal issues or Anarch assault before the latter move in. As often as not, the Anarchs cannot agree on a form of government or move to establish control over organized crime as their primary method of revenue as well as influence. When the dust settles and more idealistic forms of Anarch government have been discredited, the remaining Anarchs appoint the local crime lord or lady as the Baron.<br /> <br /> This sounds like a specific story but it's actually happened a dozen or more times among successful Anarch takeovers. It turns out money, guns, and blood trafficking (with or without the Kine still attached to it) are how a domain keeps the lights on. Simply put, if you know how to run a criminal organization, you know how to run a city's Kindred. More idealistic Anarchs may not like when organized crime takes over but they at least have the means to protect the Masquerade, get Neonates out of jail before sunrise, and dispose of bodies. The fact so many Anarchs are recruited from gangs makes them the equals but opposites of Coplands.<br /> <br /> Cynically, many believe Kleptocracies are inevitably going to fall in line with the Camarilla's ethos but this is rarely the case. While organized crime is something the Camarilla routinely controls, most kleptocracies take a Miltonian &quot;It is better to reign in Hell&quot; view or, more precisely, &quot;better to be a big fish in a smaller pond.&quot; Few of them would be Princes or even Primogen in cities not run by Anarchs and enjoy most of the privileges of both in their domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-15-2022, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum