uation across the world. Those with the skills and the tools to cross information brought by members and found in the web (or their own databases) can piece together the secrets and going ons, follow the trails of Prestation, the gossips of Elysiums and pierce layers of secrecy over the true goals of Princes all over the place, while those who deem themselves authority on the physical world are none the wiser.<br /> <br /> The Network Domain can do more than offer a place and information to its members. It ships resources and place people, it pools ideas and expertise, it makes the political chess of the entire world easy to visualize and understand, it filters Disciplines and generation out of the social totem pole, it coordinates agents and servitors. And if the Prince itself finds out what's going on? What will they do, join the community as a <i>noob</i>?<br /> <br /> Distinctly from most Anarch Domains, Network Domains have a lot of Titles. Administrators, moderators, record keepers, fact-checkers, Anime Gif Creators, everything goes and can be coded directly in the system, so there's never doubt about who's the title holder. There are public and private spaces, each with their own encryption, and systems of layered and/or parallel hierarchies behind the initial facade of equality, ripe for exploration for those who learn to master the social system. Some are clearly structured and at the hands of the app's owners, others are wild spaces maintained by invisible watchers, and others still are bold enough to have Open Code, playing straight with the digital system, but in the hands of Kindred that specialized in gaming on-line social dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOooo, this is a really interesting idea and reminds me of the idea I had of adapting the Dread Pirate Roberts and the Silk Road from RL (the drug trafficking network) to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Except it would be an Anarch version of the Circulatory System.<br /> <br /> As long as you have the cash, they have the blood.<br /> <br /> Just don't question where it comes from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:49:33-07:00","id":1486584,"title":"","content":"I can really see some naturally born domains.<br /> <br /> Smaller satellite towns around bigger Camarilla cities, that works almost as an Anarch embassy or common house(s). And those Anarchs that live there are pretty much accustomed with Kindred coming and going. And are somewhat well informed with what happens in the Cam territory, maybe have some contacts with Sheriff or Seneschal.<br /> <br /> <br /> A nice one would be a &quot;Gangrel's Rule&quot; (or werewolves rules if you like) Anarch domain, where you do what you can get away with. Can't protect your territory? Goddamn, you don't deserve it. We have some really hard disputes? Let's go talk with the eldest (or strongest alpha) of the city to see what we are gonna do about it. Wow, seems like we have some personal problems with our neighbors... better challenge their chief for a monomacy. Or a hunting challenge. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also like to think there might be some even more feudal and reactionary domains than Camarilla's. Like, it is full-on peasants, knights, kings and all that, blood tax (requiem style, which by the way has a ton of fun different princes types), calls for war... But also, feasts, grand courts and tournaments. It probably is envision and maintained by one or a coterie of really rich and mad Kindred.<br /> Which makes me think there might be some cities that are really close to Camarilla in some ways, but don't actually want to be part of it, or have some critical problem with one of its points. So they actually have some good relationship with adjacent Camarilla domains but aren't part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}